.TH RMDIR "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
rmdir \- remove empty directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rmdir
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... \fI\,DIRECTORY\/\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Remove the DIRECTORY(ies), if they are empty.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#rmdir--ignore-fail-on-non-empty'\fB\-\-ignore\-fail\-on\-non\-empty\fP\X'tty: link'
ignore each failure to remove a non\-empty directory
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#rmdir-p'\fB\-p, \-\-parents\fP\X'tty: link'
remove DIRECTORY and its ancestors;
e.g., 'rmdir \fB\-p\fR a/b' is similar to 'rmdir a/b a'
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#rmdir-v'\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fP\X'tty: link'
output a diagnostic for every directory processed
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/rmdir#rmdir--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/rmdir#rmdir--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
